===Determiner===
{{head|en|determiner|cat2=demonstrative determiners}}

# {{lb|en|demonstrative}} Like this, that, these, those; used to make a comparison with something implied by context.
#: {{ux|en|I’ve never seen '''such''' clouds in the sky before.&emsp; }}
#: {{ux|en|Really? Unfortunately, my mind refuses to bring any '''such''' memory forward.}}
#: {{ux|en|After "reiterate" do not use "(yet) again" and other '''such''' expressions.}}
#: {{ux|en|Why would you do '''such''' a thing?}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=2|passage=I had occasion […] to make a somewhat long business trip to Chicago, and on my return […] I found Farrar awaiting me in the railway station. He smiled his wonted fraction by way of greeting, […], and finally leading me to his buggy, turned and drove out of town. I was completely mystified at '''such''' an unusual proceeding.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=2|passage=She was a fat, round little woman, richly apparelled in velvet and lace, {{...}}; and the way she laughed, cackling like a hen, the way she talked to the waiters and the maid,{{nb...}}—all these unexpected phenomena impelled one to hysterical mirth, and made one class her with '''such''' immortally ludicrous types as Ally Sloper, the Widow Twankey, or Miss Moucher.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Annabelle du Fouet|title=Weather Balloons Make Rotten Sex Toys|publisher=w:Ellora's Cave|isbn=1419954830|chapter=The murky world from whence it all came|chapter_number=2|page=49|text=Adopting '''such''' titles as “Wild Bill” and “Pecos Pete,” Canadian dominants began practicing their craft and soon attracted throngs of adoring submissives.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|title=A better waterworks|date=2013-06-01|volume=407|issue=8838
|page=5 (Technology Quarterly)
|url=http://www.economist.com/news/technology-quarterly/21578526-medical-technology-artificial-kidneys-are-getting-closer-becoming-clinical| passage=An artificial kidney these days still means a refrigerator-sized dialysis machine. '''Such''' devices mimic the way real kidneys cleanse blood and eject impurities and surplus water as urine.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170625180618/http://www.economist.com:80/news/technology-quarterly/21578526-medical-technology-artificial-kidneys-are-getting-closer-becoming-clinical|archivedate=25 June 2017}}
# {{lb|en|particularly used in formal documents}} Any.
#: {{ux|en|the above address or at '''such''' other address as may be provided}}
# {{lb|en|degree}} {{non-gloss|Used as an [[intensifier]] roughly equivalent to ''[[very]] [[much]] (of)'', ''[[quite]]'' or ''[[rather]]''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Unfortunately, it wasn't '''such''' a good holiday as we thought it would be.}}
#: {{ux|en|I spent '''such''' [[a lot]] [[last night]] (that) now I can't even afford a burger.}}
#: {{ux|en|The party was '''such''' a bore.}}
#: {{ux|en|You're all '''such''' kind people!}}
#: {{ux|en|Why, I was absolutely spellbound. She sings with '''such''' passion!}}
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=1|passage=They burned the old gun that used to stand in the dark corner up in the garret, close to the stuffed fox that always grinned so fiercely. Perhaps the reason why he seemed in '''such''' a ghastly rage was that he did not come by his death fairly. Otherwise his pelt would not have been so perfect. And why else was he put away up there out of sight?—and so magnificent a brush as he had too.{{nb...}}.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=4|passage=Mr. Cooke at once began a tirade against the residents of Asquith for permitting a sandy and generally disgraceful condition of the roads. So roundly did he vituperate the inn management in particular, and with '''such''' a loud flow of words, that I trembled lest he should be heard on the veranda.}}
#* {{RQ:Heyer Unknown Ajax|chapter=1| passage=Charles had not been employed above six months at Darracott Place, but he was not '''such''' a whopstraw as to make the least noise in the performance of his duties when his lordship was out of humour.}}
